Operating Model (How we’ll work)
I take lead on scope, implementation sequence, and technical decisions.
For each feature slice: Build -> Self-test -> You validate -> GitHub push.
We do small, shippable increments (no giant dump at the end).
Every day ends with:
working build,
tested features,
short changelog,
next-day plan.
GitHub Workflow (clean and professional)
Branch strategy:
main = stable validated code only
dev = integration branch
feature branches: feat/<module>-<short-name>
Per slice:
Create feature branch
Implement + tests
Local verification checklist
You validate
Merge to dev
Tagged milestone merges to main (v0.1, v0.2, etc.)
Commit style:
feat: ..., fix: ..., chore: ..., test: ..., docs: ...
PR template includes: scope, screenshots, test steps, risks.
15-Day Development Plan (Execution First)
Phase A — Foundation + System Skeleton (Day 1-3)
Focus first: architecture and core plumbing so later work is fast.

Day 1:
Repo setup (frontend, backend, shared types)
Env config, lint/format/test setup, CI pipeline
Auth + role model scaffold (Owner, Front Desk, Housekeeping, F&B)
Day 2:
Core DB schema (hotel, guest, stay, request, offer, event, automation_rule)
Multi-tenant model (hotel_id everywhere)
Seed data + migration flow
Day 3:
Event bus/job runner setup
WhatsApp inbound/outbound adapter interface (provider-agnostic)
Audit logging foundation
Output: stable foundation + deployable skeleton.

Phase B — Ops Core (Day 4-6)
Focus: Service Request System (highest operational value + fastest pilot trust).

Omni intake: WhatsApp + manual front desk + QR form
Routing engine (rule-based department mapping)
SLA timers + escalations
Staff PWA task list (accept/complete/escalate)
Guest acknowledgement messages
Output: full request lifecycle live.

Phase C — Revenue Core (Day 7-9)
Focus: first two monetization automations.

Automation 1: Pre-arrival upgrade offer
Automation 2: Late checkout offer
Offer accept/decline flow + revenue event logging
Basic anti-spam guardrails (message caps/time windows)
Output: measurable upsell loop in production-like state.

Phase D — Intelligence + Reporting (Day 10-12)
Focus: actionable visibility and staff enablement.

Management dashboard v1
open requests, SLA %, offers sent/accepted, revenue captured
Night audit report generation + WhatsApp delivery
SOP assistant v1
doc upload, chunking/embeddings, grounded Q&A with source snippets
Output: owner visibility + staff knowledge support.

Phase E — Hardening + Pilot Readiness (Day 13-15)
Focus: reliability and go-live confidence.

RBAC tightening + permissions checks
Error handling/retries + fallback templates for AI failures
Full E2E regression pass (critical flows)
Pilot onboarding screens + config defaults
Launch package:
runbook, validation checklist, known limitations, v1 tag
Output: pilot-ready release candidate (v1.0-pilot).

Daily Step-by-Step Delivery Loop
For every day and feature slice:

Lock slice scope (small and clear)
Build implementation
Unit + integration tests
Manual E2E smoke test
Share what changed + how to validate
You validate
Fix feedback quickly
Merge/push + tag milestone
What We Focus On First (Priority Order)
Request routing + SLA system (core ops pain)
Upgrade + late checkout automations (quick revenue proof)
Dashboard + night audit (manager trust + visibility)
SOP assistant (staff productivity layer)
Polish/hardening (for pilot confidence)
Quality Gates (non-negotiable)
No feature merged without:
passing tests,
manual validation steps documented,
rollback approach,
audit log visibility.
No release push without:
full smoke pass,
zero blocker bugs,
your approval.


